Description: EDITION ONLY: decode 3D video in software rather than copy it back for its conversion
 .
 A 3D packing other than left-first side by side is rearranged into
 full side by side by a copy in system memory, so frames of a hardware
 decoder that the output could have used directly were copied back
 first: copy-back by default, which the edition takes only by choice.
 .
 The automatic stereo filter now asks for software decoding when such a
 frame arrives in GPU memory. The player asks the decoder
 (VDCTRL_SOFTWARE_FRAMES), which switches to software only when its
 hardware decoder came from an automatic mode and copying back is not
 allowed. Either way the player decodes again from the keyframe before
 that picture with an exact seek, as a change of --hwdec does, so no
 picture is lost. A hardware decoder the person chose, or copying back
 the person or the machine's record allowed, keeps the copy as before.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
